[31m-Use this package to easily convert various time formats to milliseconds.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Examples[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-ms('2 days')  // 172800000[m
[31m-ms('1d')      // 86400000[m
[31m-ms('10h')     // 36000000[m
[31m-ms('2.5 hrs') // 9000000[m
[31m-ms('2h')      // 7200000[m
[31m-ms('1m')      // 60000[m
[31m-ms('5s')      // 5000[m
[31m-ms('1y')      // 31557600000[m
[31m-ms('100')     // 100[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Convert from milliseconds[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-ms(60000)             // "1m"[m
[31m-ms(2 * 60000)         // "2m"[m
[31m-ms(ms('10 hours'))    // "10h"[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Time format written-out[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-ms(60000, { long: true })             // "1 minute"[m
[31m-ms(2 * 60000, { long: true })         // "2 minutes"[m
[31m-ms(ms('10 hours'), { long: true })    // "10 hours"[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Features[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Works both in [node](https://nodejs.org) and in the browser.[m
[31m-- If a number is supplied to `ms`, a string with a unit is returned.[m
[31m-- If a string that contains the number is supplied, it returns it as a number (e.g.: it returns `100` for `'100'`).[m
[31m-- If you pass a string with a number and a valid unit, the number of equivalent ms is returned.[m
[31m-[m
